var e={id:`8.1.6381.5`,version:`8.1`,name:`Season 8`,date:`2021-01-26`,source:`https://smite.fandom.com/wiki/SMITE_Version_8.1.6381.5`,summary:``,gods:[{id:`agni`,name:`Agni`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Similar to some other items we have discussed, Combustion has a much different strength when Agni can hit minions versus fighting gods directly. Generating additional stacks when hitting gods helps Agni players who can land Basic Attacks during a hectic fight.`,groups:[{ability:`combustion`,name:`Combustion`,changes:[{text:`Basic Attacking a god now provides 2 stacks.`}]}]},{id:`bakasura`,name:`Bakasura`,verdict:`nerf`,quote:`Bakasura, Ra, and Poseidon are seeing nerfs to their Movement Speed. In Season 8 Movement Speed is stronger than ever due to a larger Conquest map. We looked at all gods and their Movement Speed and wanted to only nerf already high performing gods rather than blanket nerfing a wide array of gods without everyone having a chance to develop their own metas. These gods likely could use nerfs to begin with and are gods we would have expected to excel even more in a Season 8 world.`,groups:[{ability:`insatiable_hunger`,name:`Insatiable Hunger`,changes:[{stat:`Movement Speed`,old:`7%`,new:`5% per stack`}]}]},{id:`chernobog`,name:`Chernobog`,verdict:`buff`,quote:`Vicious Barrage scales on both Attack Speed and Duration, effectively making it a very weak level 1 stim but allowing it to even out with other stims by level 20. Decreasing its Mana cost and increasing its base Attack Speed help to even out its power through its ranks while allowing Chernobog players more flexibility when choosing to use this ability.`,groups:[{ability:`vicious_barrage`,name:`Vicious Barrage`,changes:[{stat:`Attack Speed`,old:`20/30/40/50/60%`,new:`40/45/50/55/60%`},{stat:`Mana cost`,old:`70/90`,new:`60/80`}]}]},{id:`chiron`,name:`Chiron`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Chiron’s Passive provides strong regen but often lacks the impact of other Passives. Herbal Medicine will now provide Power to allies being healed, giving it that extra kick for Chiron and his allies`,groups:[{ability:`herbal_medicine`,name:`Herbal Medicine`,changes:[{text:`Provides Power to allies being healed.`,note:`5 (+1 per level) Physical Power 10 (+2 per Level) Magical Power.`}]}]},{id:`chronos`,name:`Chronos`,verdict:`buff`,quote:`Chronos and Sol are often talked about with other Magical ADCs who had a very strong showing at the start of Season 7. Since then many of the core items that really boosted the role have been nerfed and adjusted, leaving Chronos and Sol underperforming. They are both gaining some general Attack Speed and Scaling on their damaging abilities to help them compete with other Magical ADCs.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`General`},{stat:`Attack Speed per level`,old:`0.8%`,new:`1.5%`}]},{ability:`stop_time`,name:`Stop Time`,changes:[{stat:`Scaling`,old:`40%`,new:`45%. (80% to 90%)`}]}]},{id:`danzaburou`,name:`Danzaburou`,verdict:`nerf`,quote:`The Legendary Tanuki has exploded into our hearts! This fun filled Hunter has been fun to watch, proving himself to be a formidable foe in his debut. Dubious Savings’ Bonus Power and the base damage of Fool’s Gold in particular make him a difficult opponent to survive against early on. We are reducing both to give enemies a fighting chance against this tricky Tanuki.`,groups:[{ability:`dubious_savings`,name:`Dubious Savings`,changes:[{stat:`Bonus Power`,old:`each pouch from 10`,new:`6`}]},{ability:`fools_gold`,name:`Fool’s Gold`,changes:[{stat:`base damage`,old:`70/125/180/235/290`,new:`70/120/170/220/270`},{stat:`damage`,old:`subsequent hits of money bags and explosions from 20%`,new:`15%`}]}]},{id:`fenrir`,name:`Fenrir`,verdict:`buff`,quote:`Fenrir is often chained down as an aggressive support or a bruiser Jungler. We wanted to give him extra scaling and better access to his strong utility to help him excel when building higher raw power. The biggest change here is Seething Howl providing 2 Unbound Runes. This allows Fenrir in the jungle to more reliably use his runes to clear while still getting access to his Stun when it comes time to gank.`,groups:[{ability:`unchained`,name:`Unchained`,changes:[{stat:`Physical Power Scaling`,old:`80%`,new:`95%`}]},{ability:`seething_howl`,name:`Seething Howl`,changes:[{text:`Immediately generates 2 Unbound Runes upon cast.`}]},{ability:`brutalize`,name:`Brutalize`,changes:[{stat:`AoE damage`,old:`50% of Brutalize Damage`,new:`60% of Brutalize Damage`}]}]},{id:`hachiman`,name:`Hachiman`,verdict:`buff`,quote:`Hachiman’s Eagle Eye definitely scared us during his development. Access to extra long Range Basic Attacks was a concern but clearly this feels fair to fight against. Similar to his last change, Eagle Eye is getting some more love. Lower cooldown will highlight this unique part of Hachiman more often. Additionally, Hachiman and Rama are seeing an adjustment to their Ultimate. Both gods could dash while exiting their ultimate, causing their animations to break and visually making them seem hitable when they land but allowing them to act earlier than intended. Hachiman and Rama will now resolve the landing from their ultimates before being allowed to act or dash.`,groups:[{ability:`eagle_eye`,name:`Eagle Eye`,changes:[{stat:`cooldown`,old:`14s`,new:`12s`}]},{ability:`mounted_archery`,name:`Mounted Archery`,changes:[{text:`Fixed an issue where Hachiman can fire other abilities while exiting the ultimate earlier than intended.`}]}]},{id:`hercules`,name:`Hercules`,verdict:`buff`,quote:`Hercules’ early game saw a heavy hit with our last round of adjustments. We want to bring up his overall game to offset this heavy hit and Earthbreaker was a solid place to bring that power back. Extra Base damage in addition to scaling will help him scale over the course of the game, bringing more Bruiser strength to late game fights.`,groups:[{ability:`earthbreaker`,name:`Earthbreaker`,changes:[{stat:`damage`,old:`80/125/170/215/260 (+50% of your Physical Power)`,new:`90/140/190/240/290 (+60% of your Physical Power.)`}]}]},{id:`izanami`,name:`Izanami`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Izanami’s Basic Attacks are weird, and that is a good thing! Her unique attacks allow her to stand out among other hunters, but these attacks did have one strange feeling. As her Attack Speed rose it became difficult to really track how many sickles were out and where in their path they were. In this adjustment we are allowing these projectiles to speed up as her Attack Speed increases, making her Attack pacing feel more consistent across the whole game. This is likely quite the buff, but one that we think will improve her overall feel quite a bit. If we need further adjustments we can address that one we have her attacks feeling fluid.`,groups:[{ability:`death_draws_nigh`,name:`Death Draws Nigh`,changes:[{text:`Izanami’s Sickle projectile speed increases as she gains attack speed. This should result more closely with her sickle returning before a second one fires.`}]}]},{id:`janus`,name:`Janus`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Janus has a long history in SMITE. When strong he often feels very frustrating to fight against, with moments of high variability in his damage output combined with strong high level utility. Over time his utility and damage have been nerfed in response to the point where he struggles to see success at any level of play. Our goal of this minor rework is to help improve this variability around his kit when it comes to damage. We want players to have a more consistent experience when playing as and against Janus. Unstable Vortex will lose its center dead area but still reward players for lining up a double hit. Through Space and Time will still bring teamwide mobility and a strong chunk of damage to anyone unfortunate enough to be hit, but it can no longer literally one shot a full health target.`,groups:[{ability:`portal`,name:`Portal`,changes:[{text:`Players falling from a Janus portal can now be damaged before they hit the ground. (Previously they were untargetable until after they hit the ground completely, which was inconsistent with other banish effects.)`},{text:`Going through Janus’ portals now has a unique sound to different it from the Blink Relic`}]},{ability:`unstable_vortex`,name:`Unstable Vortex`,changes:[{text:`Unstable Vortex now damages enemies who are in between the two Vortex projectiles.`,note:`A chain of energy connects the two orbs, showing this damage area. Enemies can still be “double-hit” if they are hit where the orbs meet.`}]},{ability:`through_space_and_time`,name:`Through Space and Time`,changes:[{text:`This ability can now only ever deal up to 75% of a target’s max health.`},{text:`This ability’s audio has been adjusted to be more audible as it travels.`}]}]},{id:`merlin`,name:`Merlin`,verdict:`nerf`,quote:`Merlin’s different stances bring unique strengths to the table. Frost slows and provides quick damage (if not a hair too quick), Arcane is large AoE and control, while Fire brings high damage if Merlin can stay close. Fire however didn’t quite hit that stated goal. Radiate in particular ticked slowly, making its impact feel delayed and was often not worth the risk of channeling it on a god. It will now tick more rapidly (and deal more damage over its entire life) rewarding Merlin who can find an opportunity to stay close to his enemies.`,groups:[{ability:`frostbolt`,name:`Frostbolt`,changes:[{stat:`scaling`,old:`60%`,new:`55%`}]},{name:`Dragonfire`,icon:`/smite/wiki/Icons_Merlin_Fire_A02.webp`,changes:[{stat:`time between ticks`,old:`0.5s`,new:`0.25`},{text:`Change from 10/20/30/40/50 (+30% of your Magical Power) to 6/12/18/24/30 (+18% of your Magical Power) per tick.`,note:`Total : 40/180/120/160/200 (+120%) to 48/96/144/192/240 (+144%)`}]}]},{id:`ne_zha`,name:`Ne Zha`,verdict:`buff`,quote:`Ne Zha, similar to Fenrir, has often found himself more of a support and it is easy to see why. Flaming Spear encourages high health, his ultimate put him in high danger requiring tankier items, and his overall scaling heavily relied on Critical Strikes limiting his build choice. We want to make Adjustments to better give Ne Zha an opportunity to build Power. Flaming Spear will now scale with power, not health. Armillary Sash can no longer crit but gains heavy scaling. Finally, Wind Fire Wheels will provide flat protections upon landing. These lower protections can mean the difference between life and death for an Assassin but would be mostly a small bonus for a Tank. At the same time we also are increasing the beads window for Wind Fire Wheels to 0.4s. Even professional level players felt the window to react, especially from point blank, was nearly impossible. Overall these changes should allow Ne Zha to perform as an Assassin more consistently rather than relying on point blank ultimates to contribute.`,groups:[{ability:`flaming_spear`,name:`Flaming Spear`,changes:[{stat:`Heal`,old:`0.75% of your Maximum Health per stack`,new:`2/4/6/8/10 + (10% of your Physical Power) per stacks`}]},{ability:`armillary_sash`,name:`Armillary Sash`,changes:[{text:`This ability can no longer crit.`},{text:`Increased damage from 70/100/130/160/190 70/120/170/220/270.`},{stat:`scaling`,old:`100%`,new:`150%`}]},{ability:`wind_fire_wheels`,name:`Wind Fire Wheels`,changes:[{text:`Increased the beads window for Wind Fire Wheels. (0.4s)`},{text:`Upon landing you gain 20/25/30/35/40 Protections for 5s.`}]}]},{id:`poseidon`,name:`Poseidon`,verdict:`nerf`,quote:``,groups:[{ability:`changing_tides`,name:`Changing Tides`,changes:[{stat:`Movement Speed`,old:`15%`,new:`10% at Max Tide`}]}]},{id:`ra`,name:`Ra`,verdict:`nerf`,quote:``,groups:[{ability:`speed_of_light`,name:`Speed of Light`,changes:[{stat:`Movement Speed`,old:`6%`,new:`5% per stack`}]}]},{id:`raijin`,name:`Raijin`,verdict:`buff`,quote:`Raijin enters and leaves the meta but has currently struggled to see much success. We want to improve the strength of his core kit rather than adjusting his ultimate, as that seems to be currently what pushed him in and out at the highest levels of play. Percussive Storm and Raiju will have a lower cooldown, giving Raijin better access to answers when clearing wave and contesting objectives. Thunder Crash is also getting some scaling, rewarding Raijin players who find a chance to use this ability offensively.`,groups:[{ability:`percussive_storm`,name:`Percussive Storm`,changes:[{stat:`cooldown`,old:`10s`,new:`9s`}]},{ability:`raiju`,name:`Raiju`,changes:[{stat:`cooldown`,old:`16/15/14/13/12s`,new:`14/13/12/11/10s`}]},{ability:`thunder_crash`,name:`Thunder Crash`,changes:[{stat:`scaling on lightning and thunder damage`,old:`20%`,new:`30%. (40 -> 60% total)`}]}]},{id:`rama`,name:`Rama`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{ability:`astral_barrage`,name:`Astral Barrage`,changes:[{text:`Fixed an issue where Rama can fire other abilities while exiting the ultimate earlier than intended.`}]}]},{id:`sol`,name:`Sol`,verdict:`buff`,quote:``,groups:[{ability:`unstable_manifestation`,name:`Unstable Manifestation`,changes:[{stat:`Attack Speed`,old:`1%`,new:`1.2% (25% to 30%)`}]},{ability:`stellar_burst`,name:`Stellar Burst`,changes:[{stat:`damage`,old:`35%`,new:`40%. (70% to 80%)`}]}]}],items:[{id:`deaths_toll`,name:`Death's Toll`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Death’s Toll provides a sustain oriented and defensive start, allowing for effective early trades. Death’s Embrace continues this while Death’s Temper focuses on going on the offense.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Restore Health and Mana for landing Basic Attacks.`},{text:`Can be upgraded to Death’s Embrace or Death’s Temper at level 20.`,note:`Death’s Embrace Restore even more Health and Mana for landing Basic Attacks.`},{text:`Death’s Temper`,note:`Slay enemies to gain additional Basic Attack Damage.`}]}]},{id:`gilded_arrow`,name:`Gilded Arrow`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Gilded Arrow allows skilled last hitters to really show their stuff. What it lacks in sustain it makes up for in long term farm and immediate offense. Diamond Arrow removes the need for a target, providing near constant income while Ornate Arrow encourages you to hoard your treasure for a large offensive boost.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Mark a minion for a bounty every 10s. Last hit to claim the bounty.`},{text:`Can be upgraded to Diamond Arrow or Ornate Arrow at level 20.`,note:`Diamond Arrow Defeating anything provides the Gilded Arrow bounty.`},{text:`Ornate Arrow`,note:`Gain bonus stats for all your unspent gold.`}]}]},{id:`leather_cowl`,name:`Leather Cowl`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Leather Cowl provides early rotation capabilities, providing speed to get to fights and attack speed to help you win fights. Hunter’s Cowl turns this attack speed into a team wide boon while Leader’s Cowl encourages your team to group up around you.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`While alone, gain Movement Speed. While near an ally, gain Attack Speed.`},{text:`Can be upgraded to Hunter’s Cowl or Leader’s Cowl at level 20.`,note:`Hunter’s Cowl While alone, gain more Movement Speed. While near an ally, provide an Attack Speed aura. Leader’s Cowl Provide bonus power while your team outnumbers your enemies.`}]}]},{id:`warriors_axe`,name:`Warrior's Axe`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Warrior’s Axe may look familiar. Warrior’s Blessing encourages brawling and trading and Warrior’s Axe looks to capture that. At level 20 upgrade it to steal heavy amounts of health away or become the Hero for your team and defend them while they are CC’d.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Steal flat health away from your opponents after damaging them.`},{text:`Can be upgraded to Sundering Axe or Hero’s Axe at level 20.`,note:`Sundering Axe Steal a portion of their current health from your opponents after damaging them.`},{text:`Hero’s Axe`,note:`Protect Crowd Controlled allies with a shield.`}]}]},{id:`bluestone_pendant`,name:`Bluestone Pendant`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`The familiar Bluestone returns! This item excels at gods who can poke and need some additional help clearing. Bluestone Brooch turns the damage over time up to 11. Corrupted Bluestone throws away the poke playstyle, encouraging you to mix it up with a large conditional attack speed stim.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Apply damage over time to enemies hit by your abilities.`},{text:`Can be upgraded to Bluestone Brooch or Corrupted Bluestone at level 20.`,note:`Bluestone Brooch Apply a % Health damage over time to enemies hit by your abilities.`},{text:`Corrupted Bluestone`,note:`For every enemy hit by your damage over time, gain Attack Speed.`}]}]},{id:`warding_sigil`,name:`Warding Sigil`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Really want to survive against a Magical Bruiser? Warding Sigil provides high defense when you are actively fighting your opponent. Sigil of the Old Guard turns you into a wall for your team while Infused Sigil turns you into a bomb for your team. Either way you will want to dive into a fight head first.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Gain flat damage reduction when hit by abilities.`},{text:`Can be upgraded to Sigil of the Old Guard or Infused Sigil at level 20.`,note:`Sigil of the Old Guard Gain % damage reduction when hit by abilities. Infused Sigil Accumulate stacks when hit by abilities. Explode for damage when enough stacks are accumulated.`}]}]},{id:`vampiric_shroud`,name:`Vampiric Shroud`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Vampiric Shroud is another familiar face. Need sustain for the early game? Vampiric Shroud has you covered, literally. Blood-soaked Shroud provides potentially infinite lifesteal while Sacrificial Shroud allows you to heavily burst if you are willing a large amount of health with each cast.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Restore health and mana when your abilities deal damage.`},{text:`Can be upgraded to Blood-soaked Shroud and Sacrificial Shroud at level 20.`,note:`Blood-soaked Shroud Restore more health and mana, and gain stacks of bonus Lifesteal when your abilities deal damage. Sacrificial Shroud Your abilities do more damage but cost health in addition to their Mana.`}]}]},{id:`sands_of_time`,name:`Sands of Time`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Sands of Time returns, allowing you to cast often and providing the mana to do so. Pendulum of Ages rewards you for staying high on Mana with a large amount of Power while The Alternate Timeline distorts space-time, providing you with an extra chance to live.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Gain additional MP5 as you get low on Mana.`},{text:`Can be upgraded to Pendulum of Ages or The Alternate Timeline at level 20.`,note:`Pendulum of Ages Gain more MP5 as you get low on Mana. Gain additional Power as you stay high on Mana. The Alternate Timeline When you would die, jump to an Alternate Timeline where you instead lived.`}]}]},{id:`conduit_gem`,name:`Conduit Gem`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Conduit Gem is for the mages who want to fight early. The bonus damage allows for deadly bursts or simply to help clear your wave. Archmage’s Gem scaling this effect to a % of your Magical Power while Gem of Focus provides useful stats for those who opt into constantly casting.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Accumulate stacks that are consumed when your abilities hit, dealing bonus damage.`},{text:`Can be upgraded to Archmage’s Gem or Gem of Focus at level 20.`,note:`Archmage’s Gem Accumulate stacks that are consumed when your abilities hit, dealing more bonus damage. Gem of Focus Each time you cast an ability, gain up to 3 stacks of focus. Fail to continuously cast and lose all your focus.`}]}]},{id:`bumbas_dagger`,name:`Bumba's Dagger`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`The ol’ reliable of Junglers. Bumba’s Dagger will be familiar to all but the upgrades give Junglers something new to look forward to. Bumba’s Spear turns you into a monster, burning through any objectives (including structures!). Bumba’s Hammer encourages in-hand and ability weaving with a hefty in-hand stim and some ability cooldown reduction.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Deal bonus damage to Jungle Monsters. Restore health and mana when Jungle Monsters are defeated.`},{text:`Can be upgraded to Bumba’s Spear or Bumba’s Hammer at level 20.`,note:`Bumba’s Spear Deal massive damage to Jungle Monsters, Bosses, and Structures. Restore more health and mana when any of these are defeated. Bumba’s Hammer When you cast an ability, your next Basic Attack does bonus true damage. When you hit with this Basic Attack your ability cooldowns are reduced by 1s.`}]}]},{id:`eye_of_the_jungle`,name:`Eye of the Jungle`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Eye of the Jungle allows you to maintain control of the jungle, giving you sight anywhere you slay a jungle monster. Seer of the Jungle takes this a step further, giving you the unique ability to sweep for wards at any time. If fighting is more your taste, Protector of the Jungle makes you a major threat while fighting on your home turf, the Jungle!`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`When you slay a large Jungle Monster, you place a 30s ward where it dies.`},{text:`Can be upgraded to Seer of the Jungle or Protector of the Jungle at level 20.`,note:`Seer of the Jungle When you slay a large Jungle Monster you gain the ability to see wards temporarily. Protector of the Jungle Gain bonus Power and Protections while in the Jungle.`}]}]},{id:`manikin_scepter`,name:`Manikin Scepter`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`If you have been around for a while few things strike fear into your heart more than Manikin Scepter. Previously only on a single PTS Manikin Scepter returns; just with more reasonable values and effects. Use the burn to melt through jungle monsters and provide and extra kick to your ganks. Manikin Mace turns up all of these effects while Manikin Hidden Blade allows the assassin to truly lurk from the shadows and wait for their time to strike for devastating effect.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Damaging an enemy applies a damage over time and slows their attack speed. This damage is extra effective against Jungle Monsters.`},{text:`Can be upgraded to Manikin Mace or Manikin Hidden Blade at level 20.`,note:`Manikin Mace Damage an enemy applies a stronger damage over time and slows their attack speed more. This damage is incredibly effective against Jungle Monsters and Bosses. Manikin Hidden Blade Hitting a target when you have not recently been hit by or have dealt damage provides a large burst of damage on the target.`}]}]},{id:`sentinels_gift`,name:`Sentinel's Gift`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Sentinel’s Gift provides everything a support would need. Health and Mana to trade effectively and gold to keep up with your team. Sentinel’s Boon keeps this up and can bring a burst of healing when it counts, sieging the enemy base. Sentinel’s Embrace gives you flexibility with your aura. Skilled Supports can position themselves to provide protection to everyone or just the individual who needs it most.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Getting an assist restores health and mana and provides bonus gold.`},{text:`Can be upgraded to Sentinel’s Boon or Sentinel’s Embrace at level 17.`,note:`Sentinel’s Boon Getting an assist restores % health and mana and provides more gold. Sentinel’s Embrace Provides a large amount of Protections split evenly among all nearby allies.`}]}]},{id:`benevolence`,name:`Benevolence`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`For supports who want to roam to provide assistance across the map, Benevolence not only rewards you even when not in lane but directly can empower you allies. Compassion will make your whole team want to be near you as you take damage for them. Animosity however is for those with a more offensive game plan in mind. Turn your health into an offensive force and tear down your opponents structures.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Gain passive gold and XP. A portion of your XP and gold gained from defeating enemies is lost to you. If an ally is nearby you provide it to them instead.`},{text:`Can be upgraded to Compassion or Animosity at level 17.`,note:`Compassion A portion of damage taken by allies is redirected to you. Animosity Your Basic Attacks deal extra damage based on your health. Structures take significantly more from this effect.`}]}]},{id:`war_flag`,name:`War Flag`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`War Flag is an old arena favorite but has strong uses for aggressive support. Empower your ally and fight together with a strong stim in between each minion wave. With a War Banner your team will be moving and attacking fast; while Spartan Flag will allow them to hit hard while standing near its placement.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Getting an assist restores health and mana to all nearby allies and provides a boost to their Movement Speed and Attack Speed.`},{text:`Can be upgraded to War Banner or Spartan Flag at level 17.`,note:`War Banner Get an assist restores % health and mana to all nearby allies and boost their Movement Speed and Attack Speed more. Spartan Flag Damaging an enemy drops a Spartan Flag, providing Power to allies who stand near it.`}]}]},{id:`tainted_steel`,name:`Tainted Steel`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Last but not least, Tainted Steel. If Healing is something you want to reduce from the start this is the starter for you. Tainted Breastplate is a new and late game Anti-heal item while Tainted Amulet turns a healers strength around and allows you to benefit from it.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Enemies hit by your damaging abilities have their healing reduced.`},{text:`Can be upgraded to Tainted Breastplate or Tainted Amulet at level 20.`,note:`Tainted Breastplate Enemies hit by your damaging abilities have their healing reduced more. Tainted Amulet Enemies hit by your damaging abilities have their healing reduced. Healing reduced this way is transferred to you.`}]}]},{id:`deaths_toll`,name:`Death's Toll`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`700g`},{text:`+10 Physical Power`},{text:`+20 Magical Power`},{text:`+75 Health`},{text:`PASSIVE – Hitting an enemy with a Basic Attack restores 2 Health (+1% of your Maximum Health) and 1 Mana (+1.5% of your Maximum Mana). Basic Attacks that deal AoE damage restore half as much for each enemy hit after the first. Can be upgraded at level 20.`}]}]},{id:`deaths_embrace`,name:`Death's Embrace`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Death’s Toll at level 20.`},{text:`2200g`},{text:`+80 Physical Power`},{text:`+140 Magical Power`},{text:`+200 Health`},{text:`Passive – Hitting an enemy with a Basic Attack restores 3% of your Health and Mana. Basic Attacks that deal AoE damage restore half as much for each enemy hit after the first. Can be upgraded at level 20.`}]}]},{id:`deaths_temper`,name:`Death's Temper`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Death’s Toll at level 20.`},{text:`2200g`},{text:`+50 Physical Power`},{text:`+75 Magical Power`},{text:`+30% Attack Speed`},{text:`+100 Health`},{text:`Passive – When an enemy dies near you gain 1 stack of Temper that provides 3.5% increased Basic Attack Power for 10s, maximum of 10 stacks. When an enemy god dies near you gain 5 stacks.`}]}]},{id:`gilded_arrow`,name:`Gilded Arrow`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`700g`},{text:`+15 Basic Attack Damage`},{text:`+50 Health`},{text:`+7 MP5`},{text:`PASSIVE – Every 10s a nearby enemy minion is marked , prioritizing the highest health minion. If you secure the killing blow on that minion you gain 10 bonus gold and 20% attack speed for 8s, and restore 20 Mana.`}]}]},{id:`diamond_arrow`,name:`Diamond Arrow`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Gilded Arrow at level 20.`},{text:`2200g`},{text:`+80 Basic Attack Damage`},{text:`100 Health`},{text:`PASSIVE – When you kill an enemy you gain 10 gold and 20% attack speed for 8s, stacking up to 3 times. If you kill an enemy god you gain 3 stacks and 30 gold immediately.`}]}]},{id:`ornate_arrow`,name:`Ornate Arrow`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Gilded Arrow at level 20.`},{text:`2200g`},{text:`+60 Basic Attack Damage`},{text:`+150 Health`},{text:`PASSIVE – All sources of gold gain are increased by 20%. For every 100 gold in you have gain 1% Attack Speed and 0.8% Critical Strike Chance, up to a maximum of 25 stacks.`}]}]},{id:`leather_cowl`,name:`Leather Cowl`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`700g`},{text:`+15 Physical Power`},{text:`+10% Physical Lifesteal`},{text:`+5% Attack Speed`},{text:`Passive – While you are near an allied god you gain 10% Attack Speed. While you are alone you gain 5% Movement Speed.`}]}]},{id:`hunters_cowl`,name:`Hunter's Cowl`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Leather Cowl at level 20.`},{text:`2200g`},{text:`+60 Physical Power`},{text:`+15% Physical Lifesteal`},{text:`+20% Attack Speed`},{text:`Passive – While you are near an allied god you gain a 25% Attack Speed aura. If you are alone you gain 10% Movement Speed.`}]}]},{id:`leaders_cowl`,name:`Leader's Cowl`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Leather Cowl at level 20.`},{text:`2200g`},{text:`+40 Physical Power`},{text:`+300 Health`},{text:`+15% Physical Lifesteal`},{text:`Passive – For each nearby friendly god (55 units) you gain a stack of Outnumber. For each nearby enemy god you lose a stack of Outnumber. Each stack of Outnumber provides 3% increased Power to nearby allied gods.`}]}]},{id:`warriors_axe`,name:`Warrior's Axe`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`600g`},{text:`+50 Health`},{text:`+15 Physical Protection`},{text:`+10 Magical Protection`},{text:`+2 Damage Reduction`},{text:`PASSIVE – Damaging an enemy god steals 25 health away from your target and restores it to you. This effect can only occur once every 10s.`}]}]},{id:`sundering_axe`,name:`Sundering Axe`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Warrior’s Axe at level 20.`},{text:`2100g`},{text:`250 Health`},{text:`+30 Physical Protections`},{text:`+30 Magical Protections.`},{text:`+5 Flat Damage Reduction`},{text:`Passive – Damaging an enemy god steals 10% of their Current Health away from your Target and restores it to you. This effect can only occur once every 7 seconds.`}]}]},{name:`Hero's Axe`,icon:`/smite/wiki/Starter_HerosAxe_T2.webp`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Warrior’s Axe at level 20.`},{text:`2100g`},{text:`+300 Health`},{text:`+35 Physical Protection`},{text:`+35 Magical Protection`},{text:`+30% Crowd Control Reduction`},{text:`Passive – When an ally god around you within 55 units is hit by a hard crowd control effect, give them a shield equal to 10% of your Maximum Health. This effect can only occur once every 8s.`}]}]},{id:`bluestone_pendant`,name:`Bluestone Pendant`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`800g`},{text:`+10 Physical Power`},{text:`+20 HP5`},{text:`+10 MP5`},{text:`PASSIVE – Enemies hit by your damaging Abilities take an additional 25 Physical Damage over 2s. (Max 2 Stacks).`}]}]},{id:`bluestone_brooch`,name:`Bluestone Brooch`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Bluestone Pendant at level 20.`},{text:`2300g`},{text:`+45 Physical Power`},{text:`+30 HP5`},{text:`+30 MP5`},{text:`Passive – Enemies hit by your damaging Abilities take an additional 25 +7.5% of their Current Health over 2s. (Max 2 Stacks).`}]}]},{id:`bluestone_brooch`,name:`Bluestone Brooch`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Bluestone Pendant at level 20.`},{text:`2300g`},{text:`+60 Physical Power`},{text:`+20 HP5`},{text:`+20 MP5`},{text:`Passive – Enemies hit by your damaging Abilities take an additional 75 damage over 5s and reduced enemy attack speed by 10%. (Max 2 Stacks). For every enemy afflicted you gain 15% Attacks Speed up to a Maximum of 5 enemies.`}]}]},{id:`warding_sigil`,name:`Warding Sigil`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`700g`},{text:`+100 Health`},{text:`+15 Magical Protection`},{text:`Passive – Whenever you are hit by an ability you gain a stack of Dampening, decreasing damage taken by 5 for 5s. This occurs only once per ability cast. This can stack twice.`}]}]},{id:`sigil_of_the_old_guard`,name:`Sigil of the Old Guard`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Warding Sigil at level 20.`},{text:`2200g`},{text:`+200 Health`},{text:`+75 Magical Protection`},{text:`Passive – Whenever you are hit by an ability you gain a stack of Rebuke, decreasing damage taken by 4% for 5s. This occurs only once per ability cast. This can stack three times.`}]}]},{id:`infused_sigil`,name:`Infused Sigil`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Warding Sigil at level 20.`},{text:`2200g`},{text:`+350 Health`},{text:`+25 Magical Protection`},{text:`+25 Physical Protection`},{text:`Passive – Whenever you are hit by an ability, your Infused Sigil gains a stack. This occurs only once per ability cast. At 5 stacks it explodes after 0.5s, dealing 400 Magical Damage to enemies within 30 units of you.`}]}]},{id:`vampiric_shroud`,name:`Vampiric Shroud`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`850g`},{text:`+15 Magical power`},{text:`+75 Health`},{text:`+15 Physical Protection`},{text:`+5% Magical Lifesteal`},{text:`PASSIVE – Damaging any enemies with an ability gives you bonus 6 health and 6 mana. Can only trigger once per target per ability.`}]}]},{id:`bloodsoaked_shroud`,name:`Blood-soaked Shroud`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Vampiric Shroud at level 20.`},{text:`2350g`},{text:`+75 Magical Power`},{text:`+200 Health`},{text:`+40 Physical Protections`},{text:`+15% Magical Lifesteal`},{text:`PASSIVE – Damaging any enemy with an ability restores 12 Health, 6 Mana and provide a stack 1% Magical Lifesteal for 6s. This can stack infinitely. Can only trigger once per target per ability.`}]}]},{id:`sacrificial_shroud`,name:`Sacrificial Shroud`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Vampiric Shroud at level 20.`},{text:`2350g`},{text:`+100 Magical Power`},{text:`+100 Health`},{text:`+20 Physical Protections`},{text:`+15% Magical Lifesteal`},{text:`PASSIVE – Your abilities deal 15% more damage, but cost 5% of your Maximum Health.`}]}]},{id:`sands_of_time`,name:`Sands of Time`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`800g`},{text:`+30 Magical Power`},{text:`+5 MP5`},{text:`+10% Cooldown Reduction`},{text:`PASSIVE – This item grants 2 MP5 per 10% of your missing Mana.`}]}]},{id:`pendulum_of_ages`,name:`Pendulum of Ages`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Sands of Time at level 20.`},{text:`2300g`},{text:`+90 Magical Power`},{text:`+20 MP5`},{text:`+10% Cooldown Reduction`},{text:`Passive – This item grants 4 MP5 per 10% Missing Mana. This item grants 7 Magical Power per 10% Available Mana.`}]}]},{id:`the_alternate_timeline`,name:`The Alternate Timeline`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Sands of Time at level 20.`},{text:`2300g`},{text:`+45 Magical Power`},{text:`+45 Protections`},{text:`+15 MP5`},{text:`+10% Cooldown Reduction`},{text:`Passive – When you would die you instead find an alternate timeline you are alive, becoming CC Immune, Damage Immune, and unable to act. After 1.75s you are restored to 25% Health and Mana and can act again. This can only occur once every 10 minutes.`}]}]},{id:`conduit_gem`,name:`Conduit Gem`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`700g`},{text:`+30 Magical Power`},{text:`+15 MP5`},{text:`Passive – Every second you gain a stack of Arcane Energy, causing your next damaging ability to deal an additional 2 True Damage and remove all stacks. This effect stacks up to 20 times.`}]}]},{id:`archmages_gem`,name:`Archmage's Gem`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Conduit Gem at level 20.`},{text:`2200g`},{text:`+100 Magical power`},{text:`+25 MP5`},{text:`Passive – Every 1s you gain a stack of Demise, causing your next damaging ability to deal an additional 2.5% of your Magical Power in damage and remove all stacks. This effect stacks up to 20 times.`}]}]},{id:`gem_of_focus`,name:`Gem of Focus`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Conduit Gem at level 20.`},{text:`2200g`},{text:`+90 Magical power`},{text:`+150 Health`},{text:`+15 MP5`},{text:`Passive – Every time you cast an ability that costs mana you gain a stack of Focus for 10s, providing 3% Movement Speed, 3% Damage Increase, and 2% Damage Taken Reduction, stacking up to 3 times.`}]}]},{id:`bumbas_dagger`,name:`Bumba's Dagger`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`600g`},{text:`+50 Health`},{text:`+50 Mana`},{text:`PASSIVE – Your Basic Attacks deal +15 True Damage and your Abilities deal +30% Damage versus Jungle Monsters. When a Jungle Monster is killed you are restored for 10% of the Monster’s Health and 25 Mana. Can be upgraded at level 20.`}]}]},{id:`bumbas_spear`,name:`Bumba's Spear`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Bumba’s Dagger at level 20.`},{text:`2100g`},{text:`+60 Physical Power`},{text:`+90 Magical Power`},{text:`+200 Health`},{text:`+200 Mana`},{text:`Passive – Your Basic Attacks deal +50 True Damage and your Abilities +50% damage against Jungle Monsters, Structures, and Jungle Bosses. When any of these die you are healed for 10% of their Health, restore 10% of your Mana, and are given 10 gold.`}]}]},{id:`bumbas_hammer`,name:`Bumba's Hammer`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Bumba’s Dagger at level 20.`},{text:`2100g`},{text:`+300 Health`},{text:`+200 Mana`},{text:`+10% Cooldown Reduction`},{text:`+10% Penetration`},{text:`Passive – After casting an ability your next Basic Attack deals an additional 80 True Damage. After hitting a Basic Attack empowered by Bumba’s Hammer, your active cooldowns are reduced by 1s and you are healed for 5% of your Maximum Health.`}]}]},{id:`eye_of_the_jungle`,name:`Eye of the Jungle`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`650g`},{text:`+10 Physical Power`},{text:`+20 Magical Power`},{text:`+15 HP5`},{text:`+20% Attack Speed`},{text:`Passive – You deal 30% increased damage to Jungle Monsters. Upon defeating a Large Jungle Monster, place a ward that lasts for 30 seconds.`}]}]},{id:`seer_of_the_jungle`,name:`Seer of the Jungle`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Eye of the Jungle at level 20.`},{text:`2150g`},{text:`+60 Physical Power`},{text:`+90 Magical Power`},{text:`+25 Physical Protection`},{text:`+20% Attack Speed`},{text:`Passive – You deal 30% increased damage to Jungle Monsters and Jungle Bosses. Upon defeating a Large Jungle Monster or Jungle Boss, you gain the ability to see Wards for 10s.`}]}]},{id:`protector_of_the_jungle`,name:`Protector of the Jungle`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Eye of the Jungle at level 20.`},{text:`2150g`},{text:`+65 Physical Power`},{text:`+100 Magical Power`},{text:`+35 Physical Protection`},{text:`+35% Attack Speed`},{text:`Passive – While in the jungle you gain 15% Power and 15% Protections.`}]}]},{id:`manikin_scepter`,name:`Manikin Scepter`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`750g`},{text:`+10 Basic Attack Damage`},{text:`+15 Physical Protection`},{text:`+3 Damage Reduction`},{text:`Enemies hit by your Basic Attacks are burned, taking 20 Physical Damage over 2s and have their Attack Speed reduced by 7%. Jungle Monsters take 2.5x the amount of damage. This effect can stack up to 4 times. Can be upgraded at level 20.`}]}]},{id:`manikin_mace`,name:`Manikin Mace`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Manikin Scepter at level 20.`},{text:`2250g`},{text:`+50 Basic Attack Damage`},{text:`+100 Health`},{text:`+30 Physical Protection`},{text:`+8 Damage Reduction`},{text:`Passive – Enemies hit by your Basic Attacks are burned, taking 60 physical damage over 2s and have their Attack Speed slowed by 10%. Jungle Monsters and Bosses take quadruple damage. This effect can stack up to 4 times.`}]}]},{id:`manikin_hidden_blade`,name:`Manikin Hidden Blade`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Manikin Scepter at level 20.`},{text:`2250g`},{text:`+75 Basic Attack Damage`},{text:`+30 Physical Protection`},{text:`Passive – If you have not taken or dealt damage in the last 5s and hit an enemy god, Jungle Monster, or Jungle Boss, they immediately take 15% of their Current Health as Physical Damage and are slowed by 20% for 5s.`}]}]},{id:`sentinels_gift`,name:`Sentinel's Gift`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`500g`},{text:`+75 Health`},{text:`+7 Physical Protection`},{text:`+7 Magical Protection`},{text:`+7 MP5`},{text:`PASSIVE – Being within assist range of a minion or jungle camp monster death without dealing the killing blow awards 7 bonus gold, and also restores +12 Health and +8 Mana. If you are not near an allied god for 20 seconds or more, this passive is disabled.`}]}]},{id:`sentinels_boon`,name:`Sentinel's Boon`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Sentinel's Gift at level 17.`},{text:`2000g`},{text:`+300 Health`},{text:`+45 Physical Protection`},{text:`+45 Magical Protection`},{text:`+20 MP5`},{text:`PASSIVE – Assisting an enemy target dying provides 15 Bonus Gold and restores 3% of your Health and Mana.`}]}]},{id:`sentinels_embrace`,name:`Sentinel's Embrace`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Sentinel's Gift at level 17.`},{text:`2000g`},{text:`+200 Health`},{text:`+20 Physical Protection`},{text:`+20 Magical Protection`},{text:`+20 MP5`},{text:`PASSIVE – Evenly split 120 Physical and Magical Protection among all nearby allied gods and yourself. If you are alone you only gain 60 Physical and Magical Protections.`}]}]},{id:`benevolence`,name:`Benevolence`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`750g`},{text:`+75 Health`},{text:`+7 HP5`},{text:`+10 MP5`}]}]},{id:`compassion`,name:`Compassion`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Sentinel's Gift at level 17.`},{text:`2250g`},{text:`+300 Health`},{text:`+30 HP5`},{text:`+15 MP5`},{text:`PASSIVE – Damage taken by nearby allies is reduced by 15%, up to a maximum of 100 damage. The reduced damage is redirected to you as Magical Damage. If this redirected damage would kill you, it does not get redirected.`}]}]},{name:`Animosity`,icon:`/smite/wiki/Starter_Animosity_T2.webp`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Sentinel's Gift at level 17.`},{text:`2250g`},{text:`+400 Health`},{text:`+20 HP5`},{text:`+20 MP5`},{text:`PASSIVE – Your Basic Attack deals bonus damage equal to 4% of your Maximum Health as Magical Damage. This effect is doubled against structures.`}]}]},{id:`war_flag`,name:`War Flag`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`700g`},{text:`+10 Physical Power`},{text:`+20 Magical Power`},{text:`+100 Health`},{text:`+10 MP5`},{text:`PASSIVE – Being in range of minion or jungle camp death without dealing the killing the blow restores 6 Health and 6 Mana to all allies within 55 units and also provides allies with a stacking self buff of 1% Movement Speed and 2% Attack Speed. Lasts 8s and stacks up to 10 times.`}]}]},{id:`war_banner`,name:`War Banner`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from War Flag at level 17.`},{text:`2200g`},{text:`+30 Physical Power`},{text:`+60 Magical Power`},{text:`+300 Health`},{text:`+15 MP5`},{text:`PASSIVE – Each time you assist a kill on a minion or jungle monster you restore 1% health and mana to all allies within 55 units and also provide allies with a stacking self buff of 2% Movement Speed and 4% Attack Speed. Lasts 10s and stacks up to 10 times.`}]}]},{id:`spartan_flag`,name:`Spartan Flag`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from War Flag at level 17.`},{text:`2200g`},{text:`+40 Physical Power`},{text:`+65 Magical Power`},{text:`+300 Health`},{text:`+15 MP5`},{text:`PASSIVE – When you damage an enemy god you call down a Spartan Flag at your location, providing 10% increased Power to allies standing in the radius. Lasts for 10s, can only occur once every 10s.`}]}]},{id:`tainted_steel`,name:`Tainted Steel`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`750g`},{text:`+10 Physical Power`},{text:`+15 Magical Power`},{text:`+15 Magical Protection`},{text:`+15 Physical Protection`},{text:`Passive: Enemy Gods that you hit have their healing taken reduced by 20% for 6s.`}]}]},{id:`tainted_breastplate`,name:`Tainted Breastplate`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Tainted Steel at level 20.`},{text:`2250g`},{text:`+40 Physical Power`},{text:`+60 Magical Power`},{text:`+30 Magical Protection`},{text:`+70 Physical Protection`},{text:`Passive: Enemy Gods that you hit have their healing taken reduced by 50% for 6s.`}]}]},{id:`tainted_amulet`,name:`Tainted Amulet`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Can be upgraded from Tainted Steel at level 20.`},{text:`2250g`},{text:`+30 Physical Power`},{text:`+50 Magical Power`},{text:`+80 Magical Protection`},{text:`+30 Physical Protection`},{text:`Passive: Enemy Gods that you hit have their healing taken reduced by 20% for 6s. You are healed for 100% of the healing reduced.`}]}]},{id:`elixir_of_power`,name:`Elixir of Power`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Elixir of Power and Defense are late game options for players looking for that final push to close out a game. While Power was strong, it didn’t fully support all build types. Defense struggled to feel worth the 3000 gold cost. Some bonus penetration, damage mitigation, and CCR will help these items stand out in more situations.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Now provides 10% Penetration.`}]}]},{id:`elixir_of_defense`,name:`Elixir of Defense`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Now provides 5% Damage Mitigation.`},{text:`Now provides 20% Crowd Control Reduction.`}]}]},{id:`shield_of_thorns`,name:`Shield of Thorns`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Shield of Thorns has polarized many players. Especially at the top end of play this item’s flexibility feels difficult to play around. We are decreasing how much damage this can reflect, lowering its impact when used to its maximum effect.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`damage reflected`,old:`40%`,new:`30%`},{stat:`cap of damage taken`,old:`150 * Level`,new:`120 * Level`}]}]},{name:`Shield of Thorns Upgrade`,icon:`/smite/wiki/ShieldofThorns_UpgradedRelic.webp`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`damage reflected`,old:`40%`,new:`30%`},{stat:`cap of damage taken`,old:`150 * Level`,new:`120 * Level`}]}]},{name:`Witchblade`,icon:`/smite/wiki/Witchblade_T3.webp`,verdict:`buff`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Now builds off Adventurer’s Blade.`,note:`No longer provides Attack Speed.`},{text:`Now provides 30 Physical Protections.`},{stat:`Attack Speed Reduction Aura`,old:`20%`,new:`25%`}]}]},{id:`winged_blade`,name:`Winged Blade`,verdict:`nerf`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Health`,old:`300`,new:`250`},{text:`Now provides 30 Magical Protections.`}]}]},{id:`relic_dagger`,name:`Relic Dagger`,verdict:`buff`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Health`,old:`300`,new:`350`},{text:`Now provides 10% Crowd Control Reduction.`}]}]},{id:`emperors_armor`,name:`Emperor's Armor`,verdict:`buff`,quote:`Emperor’s Armor brings unique utility but struggled to feel worthwhile in the many other fights that occur that are not around a structure. A boost to Physical Protection helps alleviate that feeling.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Physical Protection`,old:`50`,new:`60`}]}]},{id:`talisman_of_energy`,name:`Talisman of Energy`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Talisman of Energy could not generate enough stacks to feel worthwhile, especially in Teamfights on Conquest. This item will now generate all of its stacks upon an enemy god being defeated, vastly improving the chances to empower your team.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Now provides maximum stacks on a god death or assist.`}]}]},{name:`Jotunn's Wrath`,icon:`/smite/wiki/JotunnsWrath_T3.webp`,verdict:`buff`,quote:`Jotunn’s Wrath has been a staple but underwhelming item for Assassins. Some extra power makes sure it competes with more offensive items like Brawler’s Beatstick and The Crusher.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Physical Power`,old:`40`,new:`50`}]}]},{id:`stone_cutting_sword`,name:`Stone Cutting Sword`,verdict:`buff`,quote:`Stone Cutting Sword is a powerful tool that requires many supporting items to get its full value. The high cost combined with multiple In-hand Assassin item nerfs has seen this item struggle to be built. A lower cost frees up some gold to help support this item as a whole`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`cost`,old:`2500`,new:`2350`}]}]},{id:`berserkers_shield`,name:`Berserker's Shield`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Berserker’s Shield and Ancile existed as bruiser items that struggled to be tanky enough for Warriors and offensive enough for Assassins. These items are being shifted more towards Assassins. Both items are losing Protections in favor of additional Physical Power. The goal is that Assassin’s have options to protect against specific targets without becoming full on Bruisers themselves.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Physical Protection`,old:`30`,new:`20`},{stat:`Physical Power`,old:`40`,new:`50`},{stat:`Physical Power`,old:`Berserk Passive from 20`,new:`30`}]}]},{id:`warded_shield`,name:`Warded Shield`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`cost`,old:`1400`,new:`1150`,note:`The cost of items that are built from Warded Shield have remained unchanged.`},{stat:`Magical Protection`,old:`35`,new:`25`}]}]},{id:`ancile`,name:`Ancile`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Magical Protection`,old:`50`,new:`30`},{stat:`Physical Power`,old:`40`,new:`60`}]}]},{id:`serrated_edge`,name:`Serrated Edge`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Serrated Edge’s passive definitely asks for gods to play very differently with their abilities to maximize its use cases. The passive providing Basic Attack Power limited the pool of gods who could opt into this play style even further. Changing this to Physical Power should open this pool up.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Now provides 10 Physical Power per stack.`},{text:`No longer provides 10 Basic Attack Power per stack.`}]}]},{name:`Celestial Legion Helm`,icon:`/smite/wiki/CelestialLegionHelm_T3.webp`,verdict:`buff`,quote:`Celestial Legion Helm gives mages who are concerned about Physical Damage a strong counter choice; but the lack of Power made that tradeoff difficult to justify. Some extra Power will help this tradeoff feel more in line with other choices.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Magical Power`,old:`60`,new:`70`}]}]},{id:`spear_of_desolation`,name:`Spear of Desolation`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Spear of Desolation and Spear of Magus have similar stats but different passives, with Magus feeling like a generally stronger and more flexible passive. For gods with lower cooldown Ultimates (or for extended fights) it will now reduce ultimate cooldown a more significant amount`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Now decreases ultimate cooldowns by 8s on getting a kill or assist on an enemy god in addition to reducing non-ultimate cooldowns by 2s.`}]}]},{id:`obsidian_shard`,name:`Obsidian Shard`,verdict:`buff`,quote:`Magical Penetration has largely settled into a fine spot, but we see Obsidian Shard struggle to compete with other % Penetration options. This extra power should help it match Charon’s Coin as one of the two 20% options.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Magical Power`,old:`70`,new:`80`}]}]},{id:`polynomicon`,name:`Polynomicon`,verdict:`buff`,quote:`olynomicon is a fun item for many players but struggles to really rack up a win. A small boost to power will round out its strength and allow it to see more success.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Magical Power`,old:`85`,new:`95`}]}]},{id:`charons_coin`,name:`Charon's Coin`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Added new art to indicate which stacks are gained on the buff bar. Green “Heads” for Hp5. Yellow “Tails”/boat for Movement Speed.`}]}]},{id:`soul_reaver`,name:`Soul Reaver`,verdict:`buff`,quote:`Many players during our initial Magical Penetration changes felt Soul Reaver fought with our stated goals. It provided not only a powerful stat against tanks but a tank shredding passive, doubling down as a potent one off item. We are removing the Magical Penetration and moving it to something focused more on general offense; but are adjusting its passive and cost to highlight its identity are a % health shred option`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`No longer provides 10% Magical Penetration.`},{stat:`cost`,old:`2850`,new:`2650`},{stat:`% health damage at maximum strength`,old:`7%`,new:`9%`}]}]},{id:`rod_of_tahuti`,name:`Rod of Tahuti`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`And Rod of Tahuti is the item that is more aligned with our Magical Penetration goals. Rod of Tahuti’s cost and lack of utility passive has made it struggle to find a solid place in the Meta. The extra Penetration will make this a much more attractive option for mages across all styles of play. We will keep a close eye on this item as simply adding 10% Penetration is a large buff, but one we felt was appropriate for a very late game Mage item that has struggled compared to utility items.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Now provides 10% Magical Penetration.`}]}]},{id:`cursed_orb`,name:`Cursed Orb`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Movement Speed`,old:`3%`,new:`2%`},{stat:`Stack count`,old:`5`,new:`4`},{stat:`Magical Power per stack`,old:`3`,new:`4`,note:`15 to 16 total. Extra stack of movement speed lost`}]}]},{id:`doom_orb`,name:`Doom Orb`,verdict:`nerf`,quote:`Doom Orb and Cursed Orb bring very early speed to Mages. Not only has this become a more dominant strategy in recent months but we expect Movement Speed to be extra strong on a larger Season 8 Conquest.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Movement Speed`,old:`6%`,new:`4%`}]}]},{id:`frostbound_hammer`,name:`Frostbound Hammer`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`The Hammer Tree is also seeing a slew of adjustments with the goal of bringing The Sledge more into line and boosting unused Hammers into more relevance. Frostbound Hammer will provide some extra offense and utility in the form of its Attack Speed reduction. Pairing this with the newly adjusted Witchblade could prove a powerful combo against Basic Attack gods.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Physical Power`,old:`25`,new:`35`},{stat:`Attack Speed Reduction`,old:`15%`,new:`25%`}]}]},{id:`runeforged_hammer`,name:`Runeforged Hammer`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Runeforged Hammer is being shifted around, making it more attractive for gods who rely on higher base damages and less on scaling.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Health`,old:`200`,new:`250`},{stat:`Power`,old:`50`,new:`40`},{stat:`Passive damage increase`,old:`15%`,new:`20%`}]}]},{name:`The Sledge`,icon:`/smite/wiki/TheSledge_T3.webp`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`The Sledge has dominated the Warrior item pool, and previously we felt it needed to remain that way to ensure Warriors felt impactful. With the new Season and improved Bruiser choices we feel we can safely take this item down a notch.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Health`,old:`300`,new:`250`},{stat:`Protections per stack`,old:`10`,new:`8`}]}]},{name:`Shield of Regrowth`,icon:`/smite/wiki/ShieldofRegrowth_T3.webp`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Similar to Doom Orb, Movement Speed on Season 8 is more valuable than ever. While this nerf looks more significant the boost was already suffering from Diminishing Returns, putting it closer to the nerf Doom Orb experienced.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Movement Speed on Passive`,old:`40%`,new:`30%`}]}]},{id:`dominance`,name:`Dominance`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`To kick off the Hunter section we have a new Physical Penetration option! Dominance is a new item to the Charged Morningstar tree, providing a decent chunk of Power, Mana, and extra Penetration for your Basic Attacks. More specifically this item provides many stats a Hunter may want but not all of them in one go. We hope this item can flex into a variety of Hunter builds without enforcing a specific build that shines above other build choices.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`Builds from Charged Morningstar`},{text:`2500g`,note:`+55 Physical Power +200 Mana +20 MP5 +10% Physical Penetration PASSIVE – Your Basic Attacks benefit from an additional 10% Physical Penetration.`}]}]},{name:`Atalanta's Bow`,icon:`/smite/wiki/AtalantasBow_T3.webp`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Speaking of items that provide many stats, as a 20% Penetration option with Power, Attack Speed, and strong utility, Atalanta’s Bow dictated much of the Season 7 Hunter builds. We are removing 10% Penetration and reducing its cost to allow it to still be a strong option, but one that flexes into your build rather than determining it.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Physical Penetration`,old:`20%`,new:`10%`},{stat:`cost`,old:`2450`,new:`2200`}]}]},{id:`the_executioner`,name:`The Executioner`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`The Executioner also saw heavy adjustments in the Season 7 Penetration adjustments that resulted in it disappearing from most builds. We are increasing its stack count allowing it to provide similar levels of Penetration that it used to but requiring a longer engagement before it fully comes online.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Maximum Stack count`,old:`3`,new:`4`,note:`21% to 28% Penetration total`}]}]},{name:`8-Pointed Shuriken`,icon:`/smite/wiki/8-PointedShuriken_T2.webp`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`Critical Strike in SMITE has many fans and enemies, but we think something most players would agree with is that low Critical Strike chances randomly triggering 3 times in a row feels distinctly unfair. Going forward only Tier 3 items will provide Critical Strike chance. These items have enough Critical Strike Chance that they begin to feel fair as the players have more heavily invested into this build path with a sufficiently high chance, rather than a 5% chance from Hidden Dagger.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`No longer provides Critical Strike Chance.`},{stat:`Power`,old:`15`,new:`25`},{stat:`Cost`,old:`1500`,new:`1400`,note:`All upgrades still retain their same full item cost.`}]}]},{id:`hidden_dagger`,name:`Hidden Dagger`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`No longer provides Critical Strike Chance.`},{stat:`Physical Power`,old:`10`,new:`15`}]}]},{id:`short_sword`,name:`Short Sword`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{text:`No longer provides Critical Strike Chance.`},{stat:`Physical Power`,old:`20`,new:`25`},{stat:`Cost`,old:`1500`,new:`1350`,note:`All upgrades still retain their same full item cost.`}]}]},{id:`rage`,name:`Rage`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Physical Power`,old:`20`,new:`30`},{stat:`Cost`,old:`2400`,new:`2500`}]}]},{id:`deathbringer`,name:`Deathbringer`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`With the changes to Critical Strike in low amounts and the core of Hunter Penetration being adjusted, we want to ensure Critical Strike items provide enough late game power. Deathbringer while fun has struggled to be effective. Some extra power will help bolster Critical Strike builds.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Physical Power`,old:`40`,new:`50`}]}]},{name:`Shadowsteel Shuriken`,icon:`/smite/wiki/ShadowsteelShuriken_T3.webp`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:`All the Shurikens are also seeing a boost. Their utility often came at a heavy premium that made Critical Strike builds feel underwhelming. Some extra stats behind each item (or lowering the cost to help its overall power curve) will help them stand out.`,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Physical Power`,old:`30`,new:`40`},{stat:`Attack Speed`,old:`10%`,new:`15%`,note:`This item received additional changes outlined in the anti-healing section.`}]}]},{name:`Wind Demon`,icon:`/smite/wiki/WindDemon_T3.webp`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`Critical Strike Chance`,old:`15%`,new:`20%`}]}]},{name:`Poisoned Star`,icon:`/smite/wiki/PoisonedStar_T3.webp`,verdict:`adjust`,quote:``,groups:[{name:``,changes:[{stat:`cost`,old:`2500`,new:`2300`},{stat:`poison slow`,old:`15%`,new:`10%`}]}]}],general:[{title:`All Modes – New Healing Rules`,lines:[`Global Anti-Healing Aura`,`While not “Brawling” your Ability and Lifesteal healing taken is reduced by 30%.`,`A god is considered Brawling if they have damaged or applied Crowd Control to an enemy god (or they have been damaged or Crowd Controlled by an enemy god) in the last 4s.`,`Anti-heal Item Changes`,`Divine Ruin`,`Decreased Anti-heal from 40% to 35%.`,`Decreased duration from 8s to 6s.`,`Brawler's Beat Stick`,`Decreased Anti-heal from 40% to 35%.`,`Decreased duration from 8s to 6s.`,`Toxic Blade`,`Decreased Anti-heal per stack from 20% to 17.5%.`,`Decreased duration from 8s to 6s.`,`Pestilence`,`Decreased Aura Anti-heal from 25% to 20%.`,`Contagion`,`Decreased Aura Anti-heal from 25% to 20%.`,`Cursed Ankh`,`Decreased Anti-heal from 50% to 45%.`,`Decreased duration from 10s to 6s.`,`Cursed Ankh Upgrade`,`Decreased Anti-heal from 50% to 45%.`,`Decreased duration from 10s to 8s.`,`Shadowsteel Shuriken`,`Decreased Anti-heal from 40% to 35%.`,`Decreased duration from 8s to 6s.`,`This item has received additional balance changes, outlined in the item section.`,`Rod of Healing`,`Increased Healing increase from 5% to 10%.`,`No longer increases by 5% when taking or dealing damage.`,`Rod of Asclepius`,`Increased Healing increase from 10% to 20%.`,`No longer increases by 15% when taking or dealing damage.`,`Caduceus Shield`,`Increased Healing increase from 10% to 20%.`,`No longer increases by 15% when taking or dealing damage.`]},{title:`Jungle Camp Vision Changes`,lines:[`Gods that visit a Jungle Camp on their side of the map will now receive vision of the in-world and minimap respawn timers for that camp. This is granted even if the camp was invaded and cleared by the enemy.`]},{title:`Conquest`,lines:[`Living Conquest Map`,`In addition to the completely new 8.1 Conquest Map, there will be 3 more distinct updates to the map throughout the Season.`,`Each Update will have a specific theme that follows the SMITE storyline and god release plan.`,`Each Update will have art and design updates to the map to compliment the theme.`,`Conquest is our most competitive game mode and we want to increase its ability to receive art and design updates to levels never seen before!`,`There will still be continual balance changes to the map every update, especially as we gather data and feedback at the start of the season.`,`An Entirely New Conquest Map`,`New layout`,`Wider map from lane to lane`,`Longer map from base to base`,`Completely reworked Jungle with more variance in its paths and geometry. Some paths are especially narrow, and others are much wider.`,`New Camps and different camp locations.`,`New art set`,`Chaos side takes the form of Tiamat’s Babylonian fortress`,`Order side is a totally rebuilt Mount Olympus`,`Order and Chaos towers have completely new models`,`Chaos Titan is a completely new character`,`Chaos Minions are completely new characters`,`New Jungle Monsters – Scorpions`,`Many of our favorite jungle monsters, as well as the Order Titan and Minions will be keeping their current Season 7 art on the new map.`,`Balance`,`There have been major changes to all spawn times, jungle monsters stats, and objectives.`,`New Objectives / Features`,`New NPC – Greater Scorpion (Jungle)`,`Mid-game objectives located in the Jungle`,`Two Greater Scorpions will spawn on each side of the map, in both the Gold Fury and Fire Giant pits`,`While alive, these monsters prevent the spawn of both major neutral bosses`,`After a Greater Scorpion is slain, its spawn location will move deeper into the enemy jungle, depending on which team secured the kill`,`Slaying a Greater Scorpion will enhance your buff camps on the side of the map where it was killed. These camps drop Enhanced Buffs that provide additional bonuses on top of their base effects`,`Enhanced Damage Buff`,`Additionally provides 7% Physical and Magical lifesteal`,`Enhanced Speed Buff`,`Increases CCR bonus from 10% to 20% (+10%)`,`Enhanced Mana Buff`,`Increases CDR bonus from 10% to 20% (+10%)`,`Additionally provides 10% increased Maximum Mana`,`Enhanced Void Buff`,`Increases Attack Speed bonus from 10% to 25% (+15%)`,`New NPC – Lesser Scorpion (Lane)`,`Early-game objective for Duo and Solo lanes that spawn on the outer edges of the map`,`2 will spawn in Duo lane`,`1 will spawn in Solo lane`,`These monsters will be “downed” when their HP bar is depleted, and will require 3 more hits to secure the kill and Gold/XP rewards`,`While in their downed state, they emit a healing aura that heals 20 HP per second for a maximum of 10 seconds`,`Base Gates`,`SMITE’s first dynamic geometry is being added to the S8 Conquest Map! These doors will act like a jungle wall when closed, and a jungle path when opened`,`Each base has two doors nestled in the walls between the phoenixes and are useful shortcuts into the Jungle`,`These doors will open when a god sets foot on a specific area inside the base`,`Doors cannot be opened from the outside, but gods, including enemies, can leap or blink over walls to open them`,`Players attempting to open enemy doors from the inside will be afflicted with Invader’s Curse and will need to stand on the trigger for longer to open the door`,`Fountain`,`While all of their phoenixes are alive, Gods will now receive Reinvigoration when exiting their fountain`,`Increases out-of-combat Movement Speed by 40%`,`Lasts 5 seconds`,`This will still be enhanced by Pyromancer kills`,`Jungle`,`All Buff camps now spawn at 00:20`,`All Mid Harpy camps now spawn at 00:35`,`Increased Mid Harpy respawn time from 90 to 120 seconds`,`Jungle Shrine has been removed`,`Invader’s Curse now encompasses all buff camps until 01:00`,`Void Camp`,`Reworked Void Sludge`,`Now stacks up to 3 times`,`Applies 5% protection reduction per stack`,`Reduced ability cooldown from 30 to 7 seconds`,`Debuff lifetime reduced from 20 to 10 seconds`,`No longer lowers your targeting priority from other minions`]},{title:`Death's Toll`,lines:[`Increased cost from 700g to 750g`,`Decreased Health Restore from 1% Maximum Health to 0.75% Maximum Health`]},{title:`Death's Embrace`,lines:[`Decreased Physical Power from 80 to 65`,`Decreased Magical Power from 140 to 110`]},{title:`Manikin Scepter`,lines:[`Decreased damage over time from 20 Physical Damage to 16 Physical Damage over 2 seconds`,`Increased Jungle Bonus Damage from 2.5x to 3x`]},{title:`Eye of the Jungle`,lines:[`Decreased base attack speed from 20% to 15%`]},{title:`Protector of the Jungle`,lines:[`Decreased the passive bonus from 15% to 12%`]},{title:`Bumba's Dagger`,lines:[`Increased bonus Basic Attack damage from 15 to 20 True Damage`]},{title:`The Alternate Timeline`,lines:[`No longer provides +15 MP5`]},{title:`Ornate Arrow`,lines:[`Text now specifies it provides Physical Critical Strike chance.`]},{title:`Ne Zha`,lines:[`Flaming Spear`,`Decreased Physical Power Scaling on the heal from 10% per stack to 5% per stack.`]},{title:`Danzaburou`,lines:[`Fixed an issue where the looping sound FX on Danzaburou’s ultimate rocket would not play for the entire duration as it traveled`,`Increased the volume of the sound FX on Danzaburou’s ultimate rocket`]},{title:`Janus`,lines:[`Portal`,`Changes that were planned for this ability for 8.1 are being reverted and will not go live in 8.1. This is due to the issues it had when Janus used the ability on himself.`,`We do plan on still going forward with this change in future updates, but with specific programming to only change the functionality of the falling state at the end of the ability.`]},{title:`Jormungandr`,lines:[`Jormungandr’s basic attacks will not trigger any item effects, including all starter items and their upgrades. Previously he was allowed to trigger blessings only because the effects were limited, but the 8.1 starters create clear break cases.`]},{title:`Item Bug Fixes`,lines:[`General`,`Updated text on many starter items for clarity and consistency`,`Bumbas Hammer`,`Fixed an issue where toggle or multi-fire abilities could trigger this item. This item should behave similarly to Hydra’s Lament and Polynomicon when it comes to what abilities can proc this effect.`,`NOTE: There are two issues we are aware of that will be fixed in 8.2. Some abilities such as Nemesis Shield and Hera’s Shield will trigger this item after the shield fades. This does not match Hydra’s Lament or Polynomicon which procs immediately. Additionally, Zhong Kui’s ultimate and Ah Puch’s Undead Surge will not proc this item. We are working on a fix to allow this item to proc in this situation.`,`Starter Items`,`Fixed an issue where players could buy additional starter items.`,`Manikin Mace`,`Fixed an issue where Jungle Bosses could immune a portion of this items damage.`,`Manikin Scepter`,`Fixed an issue where this item did higher damage to Jungle Monsters than listed.`,`Diamond Arrow`,`Fixed an issue where this item wasn’t stacking`,`Hunter’s Cowl`,`Fixed an issue where this items aura could stack multiple times.`,`Leather Cowl`,`Fixed an issue where this items aura could stack multiple times.`,`Death’s Toll`,`Fixed an issue where Basic Attacks that should not trigger item effects were triggering this item. This was most notable on Jormungandr.`,`Aura Starter Items`,`Fixed an issue where the auras could remain when these types of items were sold.`]},{title:`Map Bug Fixes`,lines:[`Fixed an issues where minions were not providing any gold when damaged by towers`,`Fixed multiple issues with towers visual FX`,`Missing Invade Debuff on enemy doors and enemy jungles`,`Jungle invader curse`,`Persistent area active until 1m on game clock in the enemies entire jungle`,`Debuff lasts 5s`,`Doors Invader curse`,`Persistent area active whole game, but only on door open pads`,`Debuff lasts 5s`,`Fixed Base Door Audio`,`Allied doors open instantly`,`Enemy doors take 3s to open, and now audio cues will play to show that this is ticking up`,`Fixed an issue with fire giant where some unintended collision would remain while fighting it`,`Fixed an issue where sometimes fire minions would not have the proper visual FX or minimap icons`,`Fixed a large amount of collision issues`,`Fixed issues where god could clip into environment,`,`Fixed issues where areas had invisible walls`,`Fixed issues where some areas the fog didn’t match jungle edges`,`Fixed issues with wall-interacting abilities (Janus)`,`Pets that can travel far from their god (Chang’e and Baba Yaga) can now open doors`,`Other god pets with more combat focused and max distances will not be able to open doors, and will continue to try to go through the doors if its the shortest path, even if doors are closed`]},{title:`UI Bug Fixes`,lines:[`Fixed a variety of issues with Role Trading`,`Added Jungle Guides Art to the map`,`Fixed an issue where new Guides could not be toggled from the in game “guides” menu`,`Added a cooldown to the audio on help tip popups`,`Fixed an issue where towers were using temp icon art >:0`,`Updated Mini Map Icons for:`,`Lesser Scorpions`,`Greater Scorpions`,`Role Guide Waypoint`]},{title:`Conquest Environment Art`,lines:[`Lots of additional Environment Art decoration and props have been added throughout the map`,`Totem of Ku and tower radius should no longer be visible on the back sides of walls`,`Adjusted the floor brightness and height of FG and Pyromancer areas`,`Decreased the density of jungle fog as well as adjusted the distance effect`,`Made artistic changes to better highlight the Titan leash radius of the Chaos base`]},{title:`Additional Clarity and Messaging`,lines:[`Item Attack Speed Slows & Item Slows`,`Item Attack Speed Slows and Item Slows are strongest wins, meaning the strongest possible effect from 1 item will take priority over other item effects. This means they cannot stack. This already exists with Frostbound Hammer and Witchblade for example, but will now also extend to the new starters where applicable.`,`The Alternate Timeline`,`We are aware of selling/rebuying as an exploit case to reset its cooldown. This is technically consistent with an item like Magi’s Blessing; but given its extreme cooldown and effect it likely needs different rules. We do plan on a fix for this issue going into 8.2.`,`Known issues / upcoming fixes`,`We have a long list of smaller issues also fixed for 8.1 that were left out here, as well as many smaller ones planned for fixes ASAP like 8.2. So if you don’t see something on this list, please try to report it after 8.1 goes live.`,`Custom Builds/Auto Build will not upgrade new starters for you automatically`,`Season 8 Map`,`Adding the Spectator version of the map with reduced trees and lowered heights of certain objects`,`Doing a pass on height of trees and collision on higher objects for in-game version of the map, for gods with aerial/global abilities`,`Adjustments to rules and visual elements of new objectives`,`Additional balance on starter items`,`Scorpions are scaling health properly`,`Viewer Pass`,`;*We are actively working to get VP back up before 8.1 and through 8.1, hopefully this will be active again next week.`,`It will be using the new Twitch drop system and be a little unique to this strange intermediate time, before things get set up more permanently in 8.2`,`The Viewer point 75k reset will not happen until 8.2`,`All of 8.1 will have faster 75k skin rotations (weekly)`,`At 8.2 launch`,`Agni Skin Bundle will leave the store – new bundle will be introduced that you’ll need to buy for the S8 point boosts`,`Valkyries Bride Thor will leave the store, and be replaced with a new skin`,`The Dunk Father Odin will leave the store and be replaced by a new 200k skin,`,`We will return to the normal pace on 75k skin rotations (but new skins will be featured)`,`Other new shop changes to be shown on 8.2 update notes`,`Throughout Season 8`,`Artemis and Raijin will remain and eventually be replaced by new 200k skins`]}]};export{e as default};